From 92e570d6d0ca5fb13e60bcac3ac49027f7c17604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onlyfish <linotfish@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:02:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] audiopolicy: move Sony HAL reads and writes off the policy
 lock

Every Sony HAL getParameters()/setParameters() in the policy layer ran
while AudioPolicyService_Mutex was held. The reads were cached for 200 ms
but a cache miss still performed a synchronous HIDL round trip, and all
three Sony writes used delayMs=0, which waits for ApmAudio to run
AudioSystem::setParameters(). A slow audio HAL therefore blocked every
binder thread that needed the policy lock:

  getStreamTypeForAttributes -> AudioPolicyService_Mutex
    -> sonySet360RaContents -> AudioCommandThread::sendCommand

Add a managerdefault-local FIFO worker and turn the cache into
stale-while-revalidate:

- Write, Refresh and ReassertPlayingPkg tasks share one ordered queue.
  The producer only touches the queue under a leaf mutex; the worker runs
  client->getParameters()/setParameters() with no policy lock held and
  exits once the queue drains.
- sonyGetHalParamCached() now returns the cached value (possibly expired)
  or a miss, and queues a refresh. A missing or failed read no longer
  stalls the caller; callers keep their existing property/default
  fallbacks. A refresh re-checks the entry before storing, so a
  write-through or another refresh wins.
- sonySet360RaContents() writes 360ra_contents through to the cache
  instead of dropping the whole cache.
- sonyNotifyPlayingPkgUid() stashes the package and queues the write plus
  forced refreshes of isUpmixSupportedPkg / is_dsee_prioritized after it.
  If a refresh observes a changed value it replays the stashed
  playing_pkg, which makes AudioFlinger schedule one more routing
  evaluation against the fresh state, then stops (no change, no replay).
- The two AudioPolicyManager invalidate entry points mark the cache stale
  before evaluating, so an AudioFlinger-triggered re-evaluation does not
  keep using a value that is younger than the TTL but older than the
  event.

sonyInvalidateHalCache() (full clear) is replaced by
sonyMarkHalCacheStale(), which keeps the previous snapshot available to
callers that evaluate before the refresh lands.

Known residual: sonyPackageNameForUid() can still call
PermissionController::getPackagesForUid() under the policy lock; separate
follow-up.

Change-Id: I5e1c8a3f7d2b9e4a6c0f8d1b3e7a5c9f2d4b6e18

Patch-series squash: absorbs 0014 (HAL read cache) and 0022 (String8 build fix); content unchanged.

